Zero-dependency Node ≥22 server, ESM, built on `node:http`. Exports: `loadDotenv`, `Router`, `HttpError`, `sendJson`, `createApp`.

**`loadDotenv`** — defaults to `app/backend/.env` (README tells you to symlink it to the repo-root `.env`):
```js
export function loadDotenv(file = path.join(__dirname, '..', '.env')) {
  try { process.loadEnvFile(file); return true; }
  catch { return false; } // no .env yet -- env vars from the shell still apply
}
```

**`Router`** — regex path matching with `:param` segments; only `GET`, `POST`, `DELETE` helpers exist (no `PUT`/`PATCH`/`OPTIONS`):
```js
add(method, pattern, handler) {
  const keys = [];
  const re = new RegExp('^' + pattern.replace(/:(\w+)/g, (_, k) => { keys.push(k); return '([^/]+)'; }) + '/?$');
  this.routes.push({ method, re, keys, handler });
  return this;
}
get(p, h) {...} post(p, h) {...} delete(p, h) {...}
```
Trailing slash is tolerated (`/?$`). Params are `decodeURIComponent`-ed.

**Handler signature** — every handler is `async ({ params, query, body, req, res }) => result`. `query` is a live `URLSearchParams` (not a plain object — existing code does `Object.fromEntries(query)` or `query.get('raw')`). Returning a value ⇒ `200` + JSON; returning nothing ⇒ `{}`. If the handler wrote to `res` itself, the framework backs off (`if (res.writableEnded) return;`).

**JSON body parsing** — automatic for non-GET/DELETE, empty body ⇒ `{}`, bad JSON ⇒ `HttpError(400, 'Body must be valid JSON')`. No size limit, no `Content-Type` check.
```js
const body = req.method === 'GET' || req.method === 'DELETE' ? {} : await readJson(req);
```

**`HttpError`** — `new HttpError(status, message, details)`. The catch block uses `err.status ?? 500`, logs 5xx, and replies `{ error: err.message, details: err.details ?? err.body ?? undefined }`. Note: any thrown object with a `.status` property works (the training service does `const e = new Error(...); e.status = 503;`).

**CORS: none.** No `Access-Control-*` headers, no `OPTIONS` route method, no preflight handling anywhere in `app/backend/src` (verified by grep). A cross-origin PWA dev server (e.g. Vite on :5173) hitting :8000 will fail preflight/blocked reads unless you add CORS or proxy through the dev server.

**Static file serving: none.** No `createReadStream`, no `text/html`, no public dir. Every response is `application/json; charset=utf-8` via `sendJson`. Serving the PWA (manifest, service worker, share-target page) needs new code — and a service worker + web share target must be same-origin, so this matters.

**404 shape:** `{ error: "No route for GET /foo" }`.

