**No `FRONTEND_URL`, no `PORT`, no CORS setting.** `PORT` is read only from the shell env with a hardcoded fallback of `8000` in `server.js`. Adding `PORT` / `FRONTEND_URL` / an allowed-origin var to `.env.example` is new work. The file instructs a single team env at the repo root: `ln -s ../../.env app/backend/.env`. `.gitignore` ignores `.env` and `.env.*` but keeps `!.env.example`.

